The test concatenates two datasets along a new dimension `"sample"`, with `temp` present in the first dataset and missing from the second. In `_dataset_concat`, `concat_dim_lengths` therefore contributes one position per dataset, so `file_start_indexes` becomes `[0, 1, 2]` and `concat_index` becomes `[0, 1]`. Inside the `for name in vars_order:` loop, when `name == "temp"`, the code leaves the first position enabled and marks the second dataset's slice as missing, so `variable_index_mask` is `[True, False]`. Applying `variable_index = concat_index[variable_index_mask]` yields `[0]`.

## Answer
{"target_variable_name":"temp","variable_index_after_masking":[0]}
